            "en": "“माता पठ इति वदति,” you say. “Thus,” says Avyayaka, and he rolls round and settles, like a stone in a stream. “I thought I was nothing but a pebble,” he says. “But I am the closing of a thought, and a quote cannot be said without me.”",
